# Pairs with OnlySupersededRefused. The partition's retired floor is checked on
# every stamped append, as revision 4 of the design specified, through the append
# admission predicate. The floor is one value per partition but epochs are per
# leaf, so after another leaf's retirement a live leaf's append is refused
# although nothing superseded it (#5635). The edit is to a predicate both append
# steps read, not to an action, so it perturbs none.
MODULE: OnlySupersededRefusedFloorAtAppend
TARGET: OnlySupersededRefused
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the append admission predicate also checks the partition's retired floor

--- FIND
AppendAdmits(a) == epoch[a] >= memFence
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the partition's retired floor is checked on the append path too.
AppendAdmits(a) == epoch[a] >= memFence /\ epoch[a] > retired
--- END
